<title>INDIA: India's RBI imposes CRR on ex-pat forex deposits.</title>
<headline>India's RBI imposes CRR on ex-pat forex deposits.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India on Tuesday imposed a cash reserve ratio (CRR) requirement on foreign exchange deposits by expatriate Indians.</p>
<p>The central bank said in its monetary policy for the first half of 1997/98 (April-March) it would allow banks to determine interest rates on expatriate FCNR (B) deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
